lated Taxes Proposed Rule,=E2=80=9D July 21, 2026
. (
cms.gov
)
October 1, 2026:
New federal Medicaid and CHIP matching-fund restrictions for specified noncit=
izen categories take effect, increasing the stakes of state eligibility-syste=
m readiness. (
hhs.gov
)
Bottom Line
The most important weekly change is CMS=E2=80=99s new Medicaid and CHIP citiz=
enship-verification framework because it can transmit quickly from policy int=
o enrollment operations, MCO capitation and provider collections. Eligibility=
-system execution requires the closest attention. The next major catalyst is =
the October 1 federal matching-fund change, which will show whether states ca=
n implement overlapping eligibility restrictions without materially increasin=
g procedural coverage loss.
