<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-4" name=3D"story-4" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>4. VA oversight weakens Oracle He=
alth=E2=80=99s enterprise-execution thesis</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">GAO reported that the VA had not fully=
 implemented 14 of 18 recommendations covering cost estimates, schedules, pro=
gram management, user adoption and operational testing. The department has pr=
ovided Congress with a notional deployment schedule but not the detailed docu=
mentation or updated cost estimate GAO requested. VA nevertheless plans nine =
additional deployments during 2026 and approximately 170 sites by 2031. <a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-26-109393" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text=
-decoration:underline;">GAO, =E2=80=9CVA Electronic Health Record Modernizati=
on: Actions Needed to Sustain Accelerated System Deployments,=E2=80=9D Septem=
ber 2, 2026</a>. (<a href=3D"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-26-109393" styl=
e=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">gao.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">On September 2, the House Veterans=E2=
=80=99 Affairs Committee voted 19-0 to authorize subpoenas compelling Oracle =
Executive Chairman Larry Ellison and CEO Mike Sicilia to testify. A hearing d=
ate has not been announced. <a href=3D"https://docs.house.gov/Committee/Calen=
dar/ByEvent.aspx?EventID=3D119517" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:und=
erline;">U.S. House Committee on Veterans=E2=80=99 Affairs, =E2=80=9CBeyond G=
o-Live: VA Electronic Health Record Modernization Status Update,=E2=80=9D upd=
ated September 3, 2026</a>. (<a href=3D"https://docs.house.gov/Committee/Cale=
ndar/ByEvent.aspx?EventID=3D119517" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:un=
derline;">docs.house.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The new information does not establish=
 commercial customer losses, but it raises the burden of proof for Oracle Hea=
lth as an enterprise modernization platform. Accelerating deployment before c=
ore governance recommendations are closed increases demand for migration, tes=
ting, training, data-quality and independent-assurance services while raising=
 the probability of costly remediation.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Health systems evaluating large platfo=
rm conversions are likely to demand clearer milestone accountability, user-ad=
option measures and operational testing rather than relying on technical go-l=
ive status.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The subpoena hearing; VA=E2=80=99s upd=
ated lifecycle cost estimate and detailed schedule; and performance at the ne=
xt deployment cohort.</p>
